From b8aae513950d7fab0a4e418ca893a155730aaddb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: austin62jake <340374338+austin62jake@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:09:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): the program sim sweeps a tap at its thread's minor
 diameter

The program sim (the post gate's stock-sim clause) swept a Tap-kind tool
at its full major diameter. CAD models a tapped hole at the thread's
minor (tap-drill) size, and the tap only cuts the thread band outside
that wall, so the sim read the band as a gouge down the whole hole wall
and refused the post (a 12 mm "gouge" for an M6 tap in a 5 mm hole).

A Tap-kind tool now sweeps its thread's core, d/2 - 0.5413 x pitch (ISO
724, the depth the thread-mill generator already uses), through one
shared rule, operation::tool_law::cutting_radius. Every other tool
still sweeps half its diameter. A tap over a hole smaller than its core
still gouges, and a pitch that leaves no core is refused by name.

Partial: the tap op's own verify still judges the tap at its full
diameter, so the post stays blocked by its two "cuts past the finish
surface" warnings. That half is left for the maintainer to decide on
the issue (docs/decisions/266-tap-minor-sweep.md).

Refs #266
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
